 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Think of it like a wedding without the religion, who are you celebrating together as a couple, and what does that mean to you personally? Think of it like a guest and try not to cry. A pastor, imam, or rabbi could host it, or you could ask one of your parents. Definitely. Do something together each year, like a shared hobbie. A simple handfasting, which is like a wedding cord, or a shared cup of drink, works well. And a love story to go with it. Did you meet because of a shared interest or did it blossom after you became friends?",
